# TypeScript coding style

Applies to `frontend/` only. The always-on security rule wins on secrets.

## Updates

Copy objects instead of mutating a value the caller still holds:

```typescript
function renameCamera(camera: Camera, name: string): Camera {
  return { ...camera, name };
}
```

Do not spread untrusted JSON into state. Keep only known fields.

## Errors

Await async work and handle the failure. Do not log the raw error when it might contain a secret, token, or camera credential. Surface the existing error shape from `frontend/lib/api-client.ts` instead of inventing a new error string.

## Validation

Validate input and reject unknown fields. Use the Zod schemas already in `frontend/lib`. Do not add a new validation dependency for a single change.

## Logging

Do not commit `console.log` in product paths. Never log secrets, session cookies, RTSP URLs, or provider keys.
